}
@media (max-width:420px){.mv5 .facts b{font-size:22px}}
</style>
<script>window.MV_LP='label'</script>
<div class="mv5">
<div class="lpx-ad">Advertisement · from {{ brand }}</div>
<div class="lpx">
  <header class="lpx-hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="kick">Supplement labels · 3 min read</p>
    <h1>5 things your magnesium label should tell you <em>in 3 seconds</em></h1>
    <p class="dek">If you&#39;ve ever stood in the vitamin aisle squinting at the small print, <b>it isn&#39;t you.</b> A label&#39;s whole job is to be read. Here&#39;s what to look for, so you can check any jar in your cupboard. Ours included.</p>
    {% render 'meva-club-form', fid: 'lpl-top', compact: true %}
    <div class="trustl"><span>Nothing to pay today</span><span>30-day first-jar guarantee</span><span>UK-authorised claims only</span></div>
  </div></header>

  <section class="lpx-body"><div class="wrap">

    <article class="lpx-it">
      <div class="n"><b>1</b><h2>How much magnesium is actually in it</h2></div>
      <p>Some labels give the weight of the whole compound, like &ldquo;magnesium citrate&rdquo;. That isn&#39;t the same as the magnesium inside it. <b>The number that matters is the magnesium itself</b>, and a good label prints it plainly.</p>
      <div class="lbl"><small>Example label · for illustration</small><div class="r"><span>Magnesium citrate</span><span>500mg</span></div><div class="r"><span>of which magnesium</span><span class="q">? mg</span></div></div>
      <p>If the second line is missing, you can&#39;t tell what you&#39;re getting.</p>
      <div class="ours"><i>Ours</i><span>90mg magnesium per gummy. Printed on the front.</span></div>
    </article>

    <article class="lpx-it">
      <div class="n"><b>2</b><h2>The dose per day, not per piece</h2></div>
      <p>A big number on the front can be for three or four gummies. <b>Look for &ldquo;per daily serving&rdquo; and how many that is.</b> Then you know exactly what one day looks like.</p>
      <div class="ours"><i>Ours</i><span>2 gummies a day = 180mg. That&#39;s the whole daily serving.</span></div>
    </article>

    <article class="lpx-it">
      <div class="n"><b>3</b><h2>The % NRV</h2></div>
      <p>NRV is the nutrient reference value: the daily amount set for adults (375mg for magnesium). The percentage tells you how a dose compares. <b>More isn&#39;t automatically better.</b> You also get magnesium from food like leafy greens, nuts and wholegrains.</p>
      <div class="ours"><i>Ours</i><span>48% NRV a day. On purpose, alongside a normal diet.</span></div>
    </article>

    <article class="lpx-it">
      <div class="n"><b>4</b><h2>Which form of magnesium it is</h2></div>
      <p>Magnesium comes in different forms: citrate, glycinate, oxide and more. <b>A label should name it</b>, so you can look it up or ask your pharmacist before you buy.</p>
      <div class="ours"><i>Ours</i><span>Magnesium citrate. Named on the jar.</span></div>
    </article>

    <article class="lpx-it">
      <div class="n"><b>5</b><h2>Only the claims it&#39;s allowed to make</h2></div>
      <p>In the UK, food supplements can only make health claims that have been scientifically assessed and authorised. <b>If a label promises to fix, cure or &ldquo;balance&rdquo; something, that isn&#39;t an authorised claim.</b> It&#39;s marketing. For magnesium, the authorised list includes:</p>
      <ul class="cl">
        <li class="ck">Magnesium contributes to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue</li>
        <li class="ck">Magnesium contributes to normal psychological function</li>
        <li class="ck">Magnesium contributes to normal functioning of the nervous system</li>
        <li class="ck">Magnesium contributes to normal muscle function</li>
        <li class="ck">Magnesium contributes to the maintenance of normal bones</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="ours"><i>Ours</i><span>Those five lines are everything we say. Word for word.</span></div>
    </article>

    <div class="recap">
      <h2>Your 3-second check</h2>
      <ol><li>Magnesium itself, in mg</li><li>Per day, and how many pieces</li><li>% NRV</li><li>The form, named</li><li>Authorised claims only</li></ol>
      <p>Try it on a jar in your cupboard tonight. If it passes all five, brilliant. Keep it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="kick">If it doesn&#39;t</p>
      <h2>We made {{ brand }} to pass all five. On the front.</h2>
      {%- if section.settings.label_image != blank -%}<div class="shot">{{ section.settings.label_image | image_url: width: 1100 | image_tag: alt: section.settings.label_image.alt, loading: 'lazy' }}</div>{%- endif -%}
      <div class="facts">
        <div><b>180mg</b><span>magnesium a day, in 2 gummies</span></div>
        <div><b>48%</b><span>NRV, alongside a normal diet</span></div>
        <div><b>Citrate</b><span>the form, named on the jar</span></div>
        <div><b>5</b><span>authorised claims. Nothing else.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#5a3e4d;margin:0">And because the best supplement is the one you actually take: <b style="color:var(--plum)">soft gummies that taste like ripe red berries.</b> Vegan, gelatine-free, 60 in a jar.</p>
    </div>

  </div></section>

  <section class="lpx-end" id="join"><div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <p class="kick">{{ brand }} launches soon</p>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,40px);margin:8px 0 8px">Save your place. It&#39;s free.</h2>
      <p style="color:#5a3e4d;font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.6;margin:0">Join the No Drama Club and we&#39;ll email you the moment we launch. The first 500 members get 20% off a single jar. No card, nothing to pay today.</p>
    </div>
    {% render 'meva-club-form', fid: 'lpl-end' %}
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>Do I pay anything now?</summary><p>No. Joining is free and there&#39;s no card to enter. You decide whether to buy when we launch.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if it isn&#39;t for me?</summary><p>If you buy and it isn&#39;t for you, email us within 30 days of your first order arriving and we&#39;ll refund your first jar. <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}pages/refunds">Full terms</a>.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What does it taste like?</summary><p>Ripe red berries. Soft and chewy, never chalky.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I take it with medication?</summary><p>If you take medication, are pregnant or breastfeeding, please speak to your GP or pharmacist first.</p></details>
    </div>
    <p class="fp">This page is an advertisement from {{ brand }}. Food supplements should not be used as a substitute for a varied, balanced diet and a healthy lifestyle. Do not exceed the recommended daily dose.</p>
  </div></section>
</div>
<div class="lpx-sb" id="lpx-sb"><div><b>180mg. On the front.</b><small>Join free · nothing to pay today</small></div><a class="btn" href="#join">Join free →</a></div>
</div>
<script>
(function(){
  var sb=document.getElementById('lpx-sb'),top=document.getElementById('lpl-top'),end=document.getElementById('join');
  if(!sb||!('IntersectionObserver' in window))return;
  var seenTop=true,seenEnd=false;
  function upd(){sb.classList.toggle('on',!seenTop&&!seenEnd)}
  new IntersectionObserver(function(e){e.forEach(function(x){if(x.target===top)seenTop=x.isIntersecting;else seenEnd=x.isIntersecting});upd()}).observe(top);
  new IntersectionObserver(function(e){e.forEach(function(x){seenEnd=x.isIntersecting});upd()}).observe(end);
})();
</script>

